<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Capital Alliance lifts interim share.</title>
<headline>Capital Alliance lifts interim share.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     35.1	  vs    26.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   25.02	 vs   10.96</p>
<p>    Net asset value/shr (cts) 509.0   vs 163.8</p>
<p>Full name: Capital Alliance Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said the results for the interim period were not fully comparable. The results from Capital Alliance Bank Ltd, Capital Alliance Securities (Pty) Ltd and Capital Alliance Investement Counsel (Pty) Ltd were included for three months only as they had been recently acquired.</p>
<p>It is company policy to declare a dividend at the end of the financial year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
